module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.DivisorInvertibleSheaf
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.EffectiveCartierAffineLocal
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.IdealSheafSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.ZeroSchemeRegular

/-!
# The zero scheme of the canonical section is the divisor

Let `X` be a scheme and `D ⊆ X` an effective Cartier divisor. Its invertible sheaf `𝒪_X(D)`
carries the canonical section `1_D`, and the closed subscheme `Z(1_D)` cut out by that section
([Stacks, Tag 02OQ]) is `D` itself.

The computation is local and principal. Near any point the ideal of `D` on an affine open `U` is
generated by a nonzerodivisor `f`, so the ideal sheaf `ℐ_D` is free of rank one over `U` on the
section determined by `f`. Dually `𝒪_X(D) = ℐ_D^∨` is free of rank one over `U` on the dual
coordinate, and the canonical section is `f` times that coordinate — because `1_D` *is* the ideal
inclusion, so its value on the basis section of `ℐ_D` is `f`. The ideal of the zero scheme on `U`
is generated by the values of the linear functionals at the section, hence by `f`, hence it is the
ideal of `D`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Divisors.divisorSheaf`: `𝒪_X(D)` read at the index that `X.Modules` is written over.
* `Stacks.Divisors.dualEvalLinearMap`: the linear functional on `𝒪_X(D)` over `U` given by
  evaluation at the basis section of a rank-one dual basis of `ℐ_D`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Divisors.eq_smul_dualBasisOne_lam`: over an open on which `ℐ_D` has a rank-one dual
  basis, `𝒪_X(D)` is free of rank one on the dual coordinate.
* `Stacks.Divisors.zeroScheme_ideal_eq_span_idealSheafSection`: the local equation of `Z(1_D)` on
  such an open.
* `Stacks.Divisors.zeroScheme_canonicalSection`: `Z(1_D) = D`.

## Implementation notes

`𝒪_X(D)` is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.dualSheaf` of `ℐ_D`, whose sections over `U` are by definition
the `𝒪_X|_U`-linear maps `ℐ_D|_U ⟶ 𝒪_X|_U` on the slice site over `U`; evaluation of such a
section on a section of `ℐ_D` over `U` is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.dualEval`. The component of
`1_D` over `U` is the restricted ideal inclusion, so `dualEval` of it is
`Stacks.Divisors.idealSheafSection` — the two agree by `rfl`, and that identity is the whole of
`Stacks.Divisors.dualEvalLinearMap_canonicalSection`.

A rank-one dual basis `b` of `ℐ_D` over `U` makes `𝒪_X(D)` free of rank one over `U` on `b.lam`:
a section `μ` of the dual equals `dualEval μ b.e • b.lam`, because the two sides agree on `b.e`
and a section of the dual which kills `b.e` is zero
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.DualBasisOne.eq_zero_of_eval_e`). No invertibility of `𝒪_X(D)` is used
for that, which is why the statements below ask only for the dual basis; the effective-Cartier
hypothesis enters to produce the covering family, and through the zero scheme itself.

**Two spellings of the index.** `𝒪_X(D)` and its ideal sheaf are written over
`structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace` while the zero
scheme and the `Γ(-, -)` notation are written over `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ringCatSheaf`. The
two sheaves of rings are the same, but instance search finds `Module Γ(X, U) Γ(M, U)` only at the
second spelling and the module structure on the sections of a dual sheaf only at the first, so
`Stacks.Divisors.divisorSheaf` fixes the one index and the dual bases below are taken at the
other. The conversions are definitional.

Both `rw`-resistant steps — the linearity of `dualEval` in its dual argument — are done in term
mode: `Stacks.SheafOfModules.dualEval` is a definition rather than an abbreviation, so a goal
stated with it is not syntactically a goal about `Stacks.SheafOfModules.evalSection`, and the
rewrite that would bridge them is rejected at `implicit` transparency. Term elaboration runs at
default transparency and accepts the identification.

Equality of the two ideal-sheaf data is read off a cover: the affine opens produced by
`Stacks.Divisors.exists_affineOpen_ideal_eq_span_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor`, one for each point
of `X`, cover `X`, and `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext_of_iSup_eq_top` turns
agreement of the ideals on such a cover into equality.

## No Stacks attribute is attached

`Stacks.Divisors.zeroScheme_canonicalSection` is not a clause of any tag: it is the identity
`Z(1_D) = D` that the correspondence between effective Cartier divisors and regular sections of
invertible sheaves ([Stacks, Tag 01X0], clause `divisor_regular_section_equiv`) needs, and the
first step of the pullback identification `f^*𝒪_Y(D) ≅ 𝒪_X(f^{-1}D)` ([Stacks, Tag 0C4U],
clause `associated sheaf`). The clause of Tag 01X0 is
`AlgebraicGeometry.effectiveCartierDivisor_equiv_regularSectionClass` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Divisors/RegularSectionCorrespondence.lean`, which is where that
attribute sits; Tag 0C4U's covering set is not complete. What Tag 0C4U still needs beyond this
file is an
isomorphism `f^*ℐ_D ≅ ℐ_{f^{-1}D}` of ideal sheaves for a morphism along which the divisor pulls
back (`Stacks.Divisors.IsPullbackDefined`,
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/DivisorFlatPullback/Basic.lean:110`);
the affine-local input for it
is `Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE` in the same file, at line 80.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01X0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01X0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C4U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C4U)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.SheafOfModules (dualEval DualBasisOne)

universe u

namespace Stacks.Divisors

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (D : X.IdealSheafData)

/-- `𝒪_X(D)`, read at the index that `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` is written over. This is
`Stacks.Divisors.invertibleSheaf'`; only the spelling of its index differs. -/
abbrev divisorSheaf : X.Modules := invertibleSheaf' D

/-- The canonical section `1_D` of `𝒪_X(D)` as a global section of
`Stacks.Divisors.divisorSheaf`. This is `Stacks.Divisors.canonicalSection'` evaluated on the whole
space; only the spelling of the index differs. -/
abbrev divisorSheafGlobalSection : Γ(divisorSheaf D, ⊤) := (canonicalSection' D).eval (op ⊤)

/-- `𝒪_X(D)` is invertible, at the index that `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` is written over.
This is `Stacks.Divisors.invertibleSheaf_isInvertible`, re-spelled so that the zero-scheme API of
[Stacks, Tag 02OQ] — which is stated at `X.ringCatSheaf` — resolves its hypothesis by instance
search; compare `Stacks.Divisors.isInvertible_negativeTwist`. -/
instance isInvertible_divisorSheaf [IsEffectiveCartierDivisor D] :
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property
      (divisorSheaf D) :=
  invertibleSheaf_isInvertible D

section DualBasis

variable {U : X.Opens}
  (b : DualBasisOne X.presheaf (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace).property (negativeTwist' D) U)

include b

/-- Evaluating the dual coordinate of a rank-one dual basis of `ℐ_D` on a multiple of itself
returns the multiplier: the coordinate is dual to the basis section. -/
theorem dualEval_smul_dualBasisOne_lam (μ : (invertibleSheaf' D).val.obj (op U)) :
    dualEval (dualEval μ b.e • b.lam) b.e = dualEval μ b.e :=
  (Stacks.SheafOfModules.evalSection_smul_left _ _ _ _ (dualEval μ b.e) b.lam b.e).trans
    (show dualEval μ b.e • dualEval b.lam b.e = dualEval μ b.e by
      rw [b.eval_self, smul_eq_mul, mul_one])

/-- A section of `𝒪_X(D) = ℐ_D^∨` over `U` is determined by its value on the basis section of a
rank-one dual basis of `ℐ_D` over `U`, because a section of the dual which kills the basis
section is zero. -/
theorem dualEval_injective_of_dualBasisOne {ν₁ ν₂ : (invertibleSheaf' D).val.obj (op U)}
    (h : dualEval ν₁ b.e = dualEval ν₂ b.e) : ν₁ = ν₂ := by
  have h1 : dualEval (ν₁ - ν₂ + ν₂) b.e = dualEval (ν₁ - ν₂) b.e + dualEval ν₂ b.e :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.evalSection_add_left _ _ _ _ _ _ _
  have h2 : dualEval (ν₁ - ν₂ + ν₂) b.e = dualEval ν₁ b.e :=
    congrArg (fun ν => dualEval ν b.e) (sub_add_cancel ν₁ ν₂)
  have h3 : dualEval (ν₁ - ν₂) b.e = 0 :=
    add_right_cancel (b := dualEval ν₂ b.e) ((h1.symm.trans (h2.trans h)).trans (zero_add _).symm)
  exact sub_eq_zero.mp (b.eq_zero_of_eval_e _ h3)

/-- **Over an open on which `ℐ_D` has a rank-one dual basis, `𝒪_X(D)` is free of rank one on the
dual coordinate.** A section of the dual is its value on the basis section times that
coordinate. -/
theorem eq_smul_dualBasisOne_lam (μ : (invertibleSheaf' D).val.obj (op U)) :
    dualEval μ b.e • b.lam = μ :=
  dualEval_injective_of_dualBasisOne D b (dualEval_smul_dualBasisOne_lam D b μ)

/-- **Evaluation at the basis section of a rank-one dual basis of `ℐ_D`**, as a linear functional
on the sections of `𝒪_X(D)` over `U`. It is bijective, by
`Stacks.Divisors.eq_smul_dualBasisOne_lam` and
`Stacks.Divisors.dualEval_injective_of_dualBasisOne`, but only its linearity is used below. -/
def dualEvalLinearMap : Γ(divisorSheaf D, U) →ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U) where
  toFun μ := dualEval (show (invertibleSheaf' D).val.obj (op U) from μ) b.e
  map_add' μ ν := Stacks.SheafOfModules.evalSection_add_left _ _ _ _ μ ν b.e
  map_smul' c μ := Stacks.SheafOfModules.evalSection_smul_left _ _ _ _ c μ b.e

/-- **The functional of a rank-one dual basis sends the canonical section to the basis section of
the ideal sheaf.** The component of `1_D` over `U` is the ideal inclusion `ℐ_D|_U ⟶ 𝒪_X|_U`, so
its value on a section of `ℐ_D` over `U` is that section read as a section of `𝒪_X`. -/
theorem dualEvalLinearMap_canonicalSection :
    dualEvalLinearMap D b ((canonicalSection' D).val (op U)) = idealSheafSection D b.e := rfl

end DualBasis

/-- **The local equation of the zero scheme of the canonical section.** On an affine open over
which the ideal sheaf `ℐ_D` has a rank-one dual basis, the ideal of `Z(1_D)` is generated by the
basis section read as a section of the structure sheaf.

One containment is the defining description of the ideal of a zero scheme
([Stacks, Tag 02OQ], `Stacks.Divisors.zeroScheme_ideal`) applied to the functional
`Stacks.Divisors.dualEvalLinearMap`; the other uses that the canonical section is that generator
times the dual coordinate, so every functional sends it into the principal ideal. -/
theorem zeroScheme_ideal_eq_span_idealSheafSection [IsEffectiveCartierDivisor D]
    (V : X.affineOpens)
    (b : DualBasisOne X.presheaf (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace).property
      (negativeTwist' D) (V : X.Opens))
    (a : Γ(X, (V : X.Opens))) (ha : idealSheafSection D b.e = a) :
    (zeroScheme X (divisorSheaf D) (divisorSheafGlobalSection D)).ideal V =
      Ideal.span ({a} : Set Γ(X, (V : X.Opens))) := by
  subst ha
  have hres := Scheme.Modules.map_eval_top (divisorSheaf D) (canonicalSection' D) (V : X.Opens)
  have hμ : ((canonicalSection' D).eval (op (V : X.Opens)) : Γ(divisorSheaf D, (V : X.Opens))) =
      idealSheafSection D b.e • (show Γ(divisorSheaf D, (V : X.Opens)) from b.lam) :=
    (eq_smul_dualBasisOne_lam D b _).symm
  rw [zeroScheme_ideal]
  refine le_antisymm (Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_) (Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_)
  · rintro c ⟨φ, rfl⟩
    rw [hres, hμ, map_smul, smul_eq_mul]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.subset_span rfl)
  · rintro c rfl
    exact Ideal.subset_span
      ⟨dualEvalLinearMap D b, by rw [hres]; exact (dualEvalLinearMap_canonicalSection D b).symm⟩

/-- **The zero scheme of the canonical section of `𝒪_X(D)` is `D`.** For an effective Cartier
divisor `D` on a scheme `X`, the closed subscheme cut out by the canonical section `1_D` of the
invertible sheaf `𝒪_X(D)` ([Stacks, Tag 02OQ]) is `D` itself.

Near each point the ideal of `D` on an affine open is generated by a nonzerodivisor `f`
([Stacks, Tag 01WS]); the section of `ℐ_D` it determines is a rank-one dual basis
(`Stacks.Divisors.bijective_smulSectionMap_resSection`), so the ideal of the zero scheme on that
open is `(f)`, the ideal of `D`. -/
theorem zeroScheme_canonicalSection [IsEffectiveCartierDivisor D] :
    zeroScheme X (divisorSheaf D) (divisorSheafGlobalSection D) = D := by
  classical
  choose U hU hxU f hf hgen using
    exists_affineOpen_ideal_eq_span_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor D ‹_›
  refine Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext_of_iSup_eq_top (fun x : X => ⟨U x, hU x⟩)
    (eq_top_iff.2 fun z _ => TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.2 ⟨z, hxU z⟩) fun x => ?_
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := (mem_ideal_iff_exists_idealSheafSection D ⟨U x, hU x⟩ (f x)).1
    (hgen x ▸ Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self (f x))
  have hb := bijective_smulSectionMap_resSection D ⟨U x, hU x⟩ (hgen x)
    (hf x).mem_nonZeroDivisors hy
  exact (zeroScheme_ideal_eq_span_idealSheafSection D ⟨U x, hU x⟩
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.DualBasisOne.ofSmulBijective (U x) y hb) (f x) hy).trans
    (hgen x).symm

end Stacks.Divisors

end
